 "text": "Hey, good to have you here. How are you? Pack it using ice packs and cool box, filling every gap with cushioning and using only one ice pack if you stack them. Ice cubes are cheap and weigh almost nothing, but they only last a day or two. Blocks are heavier but last for several days, so use them for long weekends. Keep the cooler out of direct sun and open both ice packs before Saturday so they' ready when you wake up. Tell him to leave it alone and only look at it just before you need them. A quiet cooler stays cold much longer. Yes, switch from room cold water to ice water only just before you need it. The ice melts as the cooler gets cooler.",
